{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (Task ID: 5241) to implement `cmd/realpath` for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires implementing srd049-realpath requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (default behavior and existence modes). Specifically:\n   - R1.1: Default resolution - resolve each path to canonical absolute form (symlinks resolved, no `.` or `..`), print one per line, exit 0\n   - R1.2: If resolved path doesn't exist by default, print error to stderr, exit 1\n   - R1.3: `-e` (`--canonicalize-existing`) requires every component exists; error if any missing\n   - R1.4: `-m` (`--canonicalize-missing`) no component needs to exist; resolve as far as possible, construct remainder\n   \n   Two files must be created: `cmd/realpath/main.go` and `cmd/realpath/realpath_test.go`. The task explicitly excludes R1.5 (-s/--strip flag), R2.x (relative path output), and other requirements beyond R1.1-R1.4.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (`grealpath` from Homebrew)\n   - SIGPIPE handler: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main\n   - Path canonicalization modes: default (all-but-last must exist), -e (all must exist), -m (none need exist)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for comparing outputs between Go and reference binaries\n   - `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling the test binary\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"grealpath\")` with `t.Skip` if not found\n   - LC_ALL=C set automatically by the test harness\n   - Flag parsing using stdlib `flag` package (no third-party CLI libraries per D5)\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License